# Frozen first-party assets.
#
# Unlike the other manifests in this tree these files are not third-party, so
# this file is not about licence provenance. It exists because the stopword list
# decides the vocabulary and therefore every df, idf and score, and because
# stopwords.py, the asset's own header and configs/default.yaml all state that
# it is verified at load. Nothing verified it: scripts/check_vendored.py
# discovers work by rglob("MANIFEST.sha256"), so a directory without one is
# invisible to it, and a check keyed on finding manifests can never notice a
# missing one. Adding this file brings data/assets under that gate with no
# change to the script, and load_stopwords now checks against it.
acfa780187dd58c25247462c557a2a73cf9f1594b882765531c002f56c653f40  stopwords_en_v1.txt
